# Cargo package: the sum is of Buildroot's vendored, re-packed archive
# (see bmcd.hash for the toolchain trap this shares).
#
# The version is commit 4009f9c on excavador-turing/tpi branch `hive`,
# released as v1.7.0: renaming a board no longer claims to move its metrics
# history, because the series never carried a board name.
#
# Bumped here because the firmware's own pin check caught it. The check
# reports on a PR and refuses on a tag, and it flagged tpi as stale the moment
# the interface was bumped -- which is exactly the drift it was written for,
# on its first real use.
#
# v1.7.0 -> v1.8.0 (b98c5079). `tpi health` and `tpi sdcard` reach the two
# endpoints the interface had to itself, the reboot help stops implying the
# compute modules go down with the daemon, and power status reads the
# daemon's "1"/"0" rather than parsing it as a number.
#
# THE RELEASE GATE IS WHY THIS IS HERE. v2.26.0 was tagged with tpi still at
# v1.7.0 and `tests/pins-are-current.sh` refused it: tpi 1.8.0 was published
# half an hour after firmware v2.25.0, so the pin was current when it was
# written and stale by the next release. That check is the only thing that
# noticed.
#
# Measured 2026-09-12 with the pinned container: `make tpi-source` reported
# got cc486206 against a zeroed expectation, then re-run to confirm it
# fetches and verifies cleanly.
# v1.9.0 -> v1.10.0 (90c22266). `tpi network address show | apply | confirm
# | revert` -- the daemon's address feature from the command line, with the
# same rule: nothing is kept until `confirm` reaches the board at the new
# address, as a new invocation with --host. `tpi ntp` prints chrony's verdict
# per source instead of a bare "not synchronised". Needs bmcd 2.38.0, gated
# on the daemon's version the way the switch commands are.
#
# Measured 2026-09-21 with the pinned container: `make tpi-source` reported
# got db77ed3d against a zeroed expectation.
sha256  db77ed3d20ae3455726d23ebfae0b7c5461e1c3e6878e9e87d8eaa5ddfd37895  tpi-90c22266b5100a0e2f07874f6bd9e6f53b4786c5-cargo2.tar.gz
# v1.10.0 -> v1.11.0 (70953f92). `tpi network switch` takes the LACP uplink:
# `--preset flat-lag` / `trunk-lag` or `--second-uplink lag`, and
# `--replace-hand-written` for a hand-written /etc/network/interfaces (tpi#16,
# carried on as #17, by @danste22). Needs bmcd 2.45.0 for the daemon side.
#
# Measured 2026-11-20: the PR build in CI's own container (run 44708171616),
# against a placeholder line, reported got bc51e724; this is that value.
sha256  bc51e7246500b08bed73d68bdbad7db896dc7a4ae329a169c0f7cbebca4e6b71  tpi-70953f927028cdbda981d1fc5452962e51ca0ee2-cargo2.tar.gz
# v1.11.0 -> v1.11.1 (2a24029d). `tpi reboot --help` says that a BMC reboot
# keeps the modules running on a v2.5 board and power-cycles them on a v2.4
# board (tpi#19). Help text only.
#
# Measured 2026-11-21: the PR build in CI's own container (run 44955559834),
# against a placeholder line, reported got 25001bb9; this is that value.
sha256  25001bb91dff52b22340237be5d218be430d20149797cbcbae810f6446fd128c  tpi-2a24029da605be38cf3c276a37c47310924dc092-cargo2.tar.gz
# v1.11.1 -> v2.0.0 (61f83d19, tag v2.0.0). tpi checks the board's certificate
# and remembers its key per host (a self-signed board needs --pin once), keeps
# the cached token private, sends state changes as POST, and on the board sends
# the daemon's local token to 127.0.0.1 and ::1. Built on reqwest 0.13 with
# ring (tpi#21 through #31).
#
# Measured 2026-11-24: the PR build in CI's own container (run 45366845299),
# against a placeholder line, reported got 3994e243; this is that value.
sha256  3994e2435cab7c3ac05bc60c53c040a1a3f9eafe6499d7218f4c17eac5e40cc9  tpi-61f83d190b6ef670e23c2d376aa2de1b0ffd0f74-cargo2.tar.gz
# v2.0.0 -> v2.0.1 (b5d4f4a9, tag v2.0.1). The token and pin file helpers live
# once, in src/cache.rs, instead of twice (tpi#33 by @danste22, for
# BMC-Firmware#115). No change in behaviour.
#
# Measured 2026-11-24: the PR build in CI's own container (run 45456902913),
# against a placeholder line, reported got 37be7788; this is that value.
sha256  37be7788f879852fe5d0e84fad17c5f783ef69917b02423444a0fa4b2c1a3ace  tpi-b5d4f4a9f6acc1e557434c03b5f5728e857a64e5-cargo2.tar.gz
